Syslog          yes
UMask           002
Domain          __MAIL_DOMAIN__
KeyFile         /etc/opendkim/keys/mail.private
Selector        mail
Socket          inet:8891@127.0.0.1
PidFile         /run/opendkim/opendkim.pid
Mode            sv
Canonicalization        relaxed/simple
# Our own outbound mail's From/envelope domain is __MAIL_HOSTNAME__ (e.g.
# noreply@mail.sta-tw.org), a SUBDOMAIN of __MAIL_DOMAIN__ — with
# SubDomains=no, that silently fails OpenDKIM's sender-domain allowlist
# check and every message we send goes out completely unsigned (found by
# inspecting a real queued message: no DKIM-Signature header at all,
# despite a correctly published DKIM DNS record). "yes" lets it sign mail
# from any subdomain of __MAIL_DOMAIN__ too, still stamping d=__MAIL_DOMAIN__
# (the domain the DNS TXT record is actually published under) — no new DNS
# record needed, and DMARC's default relaxed alignment already treats
# d=__MAIL_DOMAIN__ and From:__MAIL_HOSTNAME__ as aligned.
SubDomains      yes
AutoRestart     yes
AutoRestartRate 10/1h
UserID          root
